# v0.24.7 — v0.24.0-next live scenario playback fixes

## P2.1 ZK proofs for high-value jobs

- New `receipt_public` Circom circuit with `receiptHash` as a public input.
- Generated `receipt_public_0001.zkey`, `receipt_public.wasm`, and
  `verification_key.json` using a fresh power-of-tau 12 ceremony.
- `ZKProofService` now loads `receipt_public`, computes Poseidon4 inputs
  with `poseidon-lite`, and verifies proofs against the exported key.
- `apps/coordinator-api/.../miner.py`: result submission generates and
  attaches a verified ZK receipt proof when the job payment is above
  `COORDINATOR_ZK_HIGH_VALUE_THRESHOLD` (default 10 AIT) or the buyer sets
  `zk_proof_required` in `Constraints`.
- `apps/coordinator-api/.../payments.py`: `release_payment` blocks escrow
  release for high-value jobs when `zk_status` is not `verified`.
- `aitbc ai submit --zk-proof-required` lets buyers force the ZK gate.
- `JobView` exposes `zk_status` and `zk_proof_id`.
- `docs/scenarios/38_zk_high_value_jobs.md` added.
- Operational note: the `aitbc-coordinator-api` systemd unit needs
  `MemoryDenyWriteExecute=no` so the Node.js subprocesses used by snarkjs
  can allocate executable memory pages.
